+/*
+ * 0101 (fix/unmap-fanout, 2026-11-24): the pages, not only the blocks. On the phone (2026-11-24 01:17-01:22) the user
+ * unmaps were 11-12 million per 30 s against 0.85-1.0 million maps: 37,000-42,500 shared-region flushes, each sent
+ * to the 240-290 tasks whose 32 MiB block bit was set (every task has filled pages in libsystem's blocks), almost
+ * none of which had that page. Each flush took every task's TLB word and queued a task_unmap in xnuhost.
+ * Now a task that fills a page of the region gets a 1 KiB bitmap of its block first (hosted_nested_prepare, in
+ * thread context before the fill takes its locks), the fill sets the page's bit under the task's TLB word, a flush
+ * sends task_unmap only to a task with a bit set in its range and clears those bits after the unmap
+ * (hosted_nested_forget). The 0045 block bit stays for a block that has no bitmap (the allocation failed, or
